::ENG4_U05_L08_GP_Q01::[MLA.ENG4.L.01] Draft: The source is credible it uses recent data. Which revision is best? {
~A. The source is credible it uses recent data.#Incorrect. This remains a run-on sentence.
=B. The source is credible because it uses recent data.#Correct. This fixes the sentence boundary and clarifies the cause.
~C. The source, credible recent data uses.#Incorrect. This is not standard English.
~D. Because recent data credible source.#Incorrect. This is incomplete and unclear.
}

::ENG4_U05_L08_GP_Q02::[MLA.ENG4.V.02] What does provisional mean in the sentence, "The board approved a provisional schedule until the final vote"? {
~A. permanent.#Incorrect. Until the final vote shows it is not permanent.
~B. careless.#Incorrect. The word does not mean careless.
~C. hidden.#Incorrect. The sentence does not suggest hidden.
=D. temporary or conditional.#Correct. Provisional means temporary or likely to change.
}

::ENG4_U05_L08_GP_Q03::[MLA.ENG4.V.03] Passage: The plan was ambitious, but critics called it unrealistic. What is the best comparison? {
=A. Ambitious suggests a challenging goal, while unrealistic questions whether it can work.#Correct. This explains connotation and meaning.
~B. Both words praise the plan equally.#Incorrect. Unrealistic is critical.
~C. Ambitious means ordinary.#Incorrect. Ambitious suggests a large goal.
~D. Unrealistic means guaranteed.#Incorrect. It means unlikely to be practical.
}

::ENG4_U05_L08_GP_Q04::[MLA.ENG4.W.04] Draft: The author has good points and says stuff about costs. Which revision is most polished? {
~A. The author has good points and says stuff.#Incorrect. This remains vague.
~B. The author is really good with cost things.#Incorrect. This is informal.
=C. The author presents a credible argument by connecting cost data to long-term financial impact.#Correct. This revision is precise and polished.
~D. The author has a lot of words about money.#Incorrect. This is imprecise.
}

::ENG4_U05_L08_GP_Q05::[MLA.ENG4.R.10] Passage: The committee gave qualified support, approving the plan only if safeguards were added. Which paraphrase is accurate? {
~A. The committee fully approved the plan with no conditions.#Incorrect. Qualified support has conditions.
=B. The committee supported the plan only if protections were included.#Correct. This preserves the meaning.
~C. The committee rejected the plan entirely.#Incorrect. It gave support, but with conditions.
~D. The committee ignored the plan.#Incorrect. The committee responded to the plan.
}
